    <!-- Header -->
    
    <main class="lesson-container py-4">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div id="tutorial-header"></div>
        
        <div class="content lesson-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <p>Networks are categorized by their geographic scope. The two most common types are LAN and WAN.</p><h3>LAN (Local Area Network)</h3><p>A network confined to a small area, like a single building, home, or office. It is usually fast and privately owned.</p><h3>WAN (Wide Area Network)</h3><p>A network that spans a large geographical area, connecting multiple LANs. The Internet is the largest WAN.</p><h3>Troubleshooting Tip</h3><p>If you can print to your local printer but cannot load a website, your LAN is likely fine, but your WAN connection (internet) is down.</p>
        </div>
        
